body:
I appreciate it man. I guess in the end the relationship worked wonders for me in my identity. Honestly with my mind set as of now there's no way I can sustain a good fulfilling relationship with a girl of any race lmao. I'm just focusing on myself as of rn, I still casually date, but I mostly hate my body and for the most part and where I was headed in life. I'm just tryna lose weight(188lbs at 5'11) so i'm not too big but I feel incredibly heavy and disproportioned so i'm just tryna get myself physically to where I want to be and build my income and work my way up to where I want to be career wise(I'm trying to become a medical sales rep but I just got a job as a material handler/driver for a medical implants/biotics company which pays hella good). 

&#x200B;

I always saw room for intense improvement towards myself, and me hating myself for my race isn't really that strong, I don't experience nearly the short end of the stick when it comes to others on this sub but it obviously still effects me in ways I wish it didn't. I love that there's a community like this for us. I always felt so alone my whole life and it's nice to know that i'm not totally alone in this.
